Scope: 
This EPD is an average EDP and applies for the following specific SINIAT produts brand developed by Etex Builfding Performace S.p.A: Montante PregyMetal AquaBoard C50/50 (or Montante PregyMetal XT C50/50), Montante PregyMetal AquaBoard C75/50 (or Montante PregyMetal XT C75/50), Montante PregyMetal AquaBoard C100/50 (or Montante PregyMetal XT C100/50), Montante PregyMetal AquaBoard C150/50 (or Montante PregyMetal XT C150/50), Profilo PregyMetal AquaBoard S6027 BA, Guida PregyMetal AquaBoard U50/40 (or Guida PregyMetal XT U50/40), Guida PregyMetal AquaBoard U75/40 (or Guida PregyMetal XT U75/40), Guida PregyMetal AquaBoard U100/40 (or Guida PregyMetal XT U100/40), Guida PregyMetal AquaBoard U150/40 (or Guida PregyMetal XT U150/40), Guida PregyMetal AquaBoard U28/28 (or Guida PregyMetal XT U28/28), Profilo PregyMetal Aquaboard S6027 BA (or Profilo Pregymetal XT S6027 BA)

This EPD was developed from data collected at the Etex Building Performace S.p.Asteel profile factory located in Corfinio. CAP 67030 (AQ), Italy, producing 100% of the total production of these products. Data refers to year 2021.
The EPD is a cradle-to-gate with options EPD and covers Siniat PregyMetal AquaBoard steel profiles. 
System boundary: 
This EPD is a cradle-to-gate with options EPD, covering the following life cycle stages: 

steel structures manufacturing (modules A1-A3), including the production of the steel rolls, the transport to the manufacturing site, as well as impacts due to energy consumption, as well as auxiliary materials, waste treatment;
transport of the steel structures from the manufacturing to the building site (module A4),
Installation (module A5), including the production of auxiliaries and of waste deriving from packaging;
emissions during the use phase (modules B). No emissions occur during the Etex Building Performace S.p.A steel structure use phase;
end-of-life (modules C1-C4), including impacts from manual deconstruction, transport of waste to treatment facility, and waste processing and waste disposal. The scenario studied considers 90% of the structure recyclable (C3) and 10% sent to landfill (C4);
benefits and loads beyond the system boundaries (D).
